**The thesis** (per the entity-gap packet, which scored Jung a PASS on the entity-gap model but green-lit the psychology-hub lane): the father of personality typing is the type system's unsolved case. The hook is the 1959 BBC scene where Freeman asks Jung his own question and Jung calls it "that painful question"; the ending is his 1957 Houston verdict, "The classification of individuals means nothing, nothing at all," followed by "Sixty-nine years later, we filed him anyway." The type is argued (5w4), never declared, with Riso-Hudson's 9w1 case given its full day in the diagnosis section and Rabbit Hole.

